#* {{quote-web|en|author=Metrowebukmetro|quotee=w:Ellie Simmonds|title=Ellie Simmonds' father: My girl has made the world stop and think|work=[[w:Metro (British newspaper)|Metro]]|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20151104181855/http://metro.co.uk/2012/09/08/ellie-simmonds-father-my-girl-has-made-the-world-stop-and-think-569187/|date=8 September 2012|passage=Speaking after yesterday's race,  Ellie, from Walsall, said: 'I would have loved to get the gold but you can't have everything. ¶ 'I've been '''PBing''' every time I swim so I can't ask for any more.'}}
#* {{RQ:Guardian|author=Owen Gibson|quotee={{w|Tyson Gay}}|title=Tyson Gay gears up for showdown with Usain Bolt at world championships|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20161018060438/https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2013/jul/03/tyson-gay-usain-bolt-world-championships|date=3 July 2013|passage="It's definitely a goal of mine because I haven't done a personal record in a long time. I'm definitely looking forward to '''PBing'''," said the American, who has run 9.75sec this year. "Hopefully the conditions will be good, my start's better and everything is working well so I can accomplish one of my goals."}}
#* {{RQ:Guardian|author=Sean Ingle|authorlink=Sean Ingle|quotee={{w|Adam Gemili}}|title=Commonwealth Games 2014: Adam Gemili keeps mind on track after silver|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20180404175401/https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2014/jul/29/commonwealth-games-adam-gemili-100m-silver|date=29 July 2014|passage=I'm only 20. Dwain Chambers is 36 now, Kim Collins is 38 and still '''PBing'''. These guys have long careers so hopefully I can push on and hope for something similar.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=James Spender|title=Argonaut Road Bike review|work=[[w:Cyclist (magazine)|Cyclist]]|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20230805223023/https://www.cyclist.co.uk/reviews/argonaut-road-bike-review|location=London|publisher=w:Metropolis Group|date=18 April 2019|issn=2050-6538|oclc=987360372|passage=I '''PBed''' my go-to twisting descent not once but twice, all the while feeling totally in control, each run thrillingly rapid but never reckless.}}

